{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"review\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Correspondence review of the clean C1 artifact (53a31b99…, executed as the latest C1 run) and the resolution of the open scope issue ef6b54abce294555b31a3c9a6ca606ac, whose answer is that the applied-state proposition belongs to claim C3 while this artifact's checker set contains only in-scope predicates.\\\",\n \\\"artifact_id\\\":\\\"53a31b99\\\",\n \\\"review_items\\\":[{\n  \\\"aspect\\\":\\\"checker_correspondence\\\",\n  \\\"status\\\":\\\"no_issue_found\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S14-recovery-start-prepare\\\",\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S11-handleAccept\\\",\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\"],\n  \\\"report_title\\\":\\\"C1 检查集已仅含范围内属性\\\",\n  \\\"report_answer\\\":\\\"该工件执行的检查集只含三条范围内属性：解析处的采纳（adopted_committed=false）、恢复者与已提交副本的向量比较（vectors_match=false）、以及提交广播后三副本的一致性（all_committed_match=false）；应用层一致性不再由任何监控器选择，因此它不再进入 C1 的判定。三条属性与已复核的对应关系一致，前置条件、身份字段、法理与驱动轮次均未改变。\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Requirement versus predicates: the three monitored properties encode the accepted C1 obligation and nothing else; the applied-state event is still printed by the harness but no monitor selects it, so the executed checker set matches the accepted scope exactly. Entry, schedule and completion: the harness is the reviewed driven version (Prepare/PrepareReply, the phase-1 restart's PreAccept and reply, the Accept and its reply, the Commit broadcast, with InstanceSpace re-read after every delivery), so the observations come from the records the handlers wrote. Oracle and identity: the same assertions and identity correlation as the reviewed three-property artifact, with the committed_reply prerequisite as admission alias for each monitor. Legal history: the prepared COMMITTED record and direct recovery entry remain declared in the claim scope. Contrary evidence and alternatives: the alternative that the applied-state observation should be confirmable under C1 is answered by claim C3, which owns that proposition and has its own reviewed check; the reservations that remain for this artifact are the ones already recorded (prepared committed record, substituted trigger) and are unchanged.\\\",\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"the harness still prints the applied-state event; only the monitor set excludes it, which is the point of this artifact\\\",\n   \\\"the prepared COMMITTED record and the direct recovery entry remain substitutions declared in the claim scope\\\"]}],\n \\\"resolutions\\\":[{\n  \\\"issue_id\\\":\\\"ef6b54abce294555b31a3c9a6ca606ac\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S20-exec\\\",\\\"S23-state-conflict-apply\\\",\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\"],\n  \\\"evidence_ids\\\":[\\\"53a31b99\\\",\\\"52a176deb66c4588a59d71f8afeb13ab\\\"],\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The issue required either that the applied-state property leave the C1 checker set or that its proposition be fixed as its own obligation. Both are now true: claim C3-applied-effect-follows-committed-vector owns the proposition with execution inside its scope and a reviewed, confirmed check (artifact 52a176deb66c4588a59d71f8afeb13ab), and this fresh artifact on the same unit carries only the three in-scope properties, so the C1 checker set as executed contains no predicate outside the accepted scope. The disputed artifact remains fixed bytes whose applied-state property must be read as belonging to C3; no C1 result depends on it.\\\",\n  \\\"residual_issue_ids\\\":[],\n  \\\"scope_limitations\\\":[\\\"the older artifact keeps its bytes; readers must attribute its applied-state property to C3\\\",\n    \\\"C3's check carries its own limitations (direct execution, one instance and key, prepared records)\\\"]}]}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-review-c1clean.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\nID=\"'$(cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport json;s=json.load(open('\"'state.json'));print([a['id'] for a in s['direct_checks'] if a['id'].startswith('53a31b99')][0])\\\") && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - \\\"\"'$ID\" <<'\"'PY'\nimport json,sys\ns=json.load(open('submission-review-c1clean.json'))\ns['artifact_id']=sys.argv[1]\ns['resolutions'][0]['evidence_ids'][0]=sys.argv[1]\njson.dump(s,open('submission-review-c1clean.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint(s['artifact_id'])\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-review-c1clean.json 2>&1 | head -10\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
